From d99415110a39edee365e289b929fa87298b31930 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Mar 2026 11:22:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Skip selinux_flags when proc attribute is unavailable

GrapheneOS adds a custom /proc/thread-self/attr/selinux_flags kernel
interface for per-app SELinux flag hardening.  On Treble GSI devices
the vendor kernel (typically Android 12-14, kernel 5.10-5.15) lacks
this patch, so the proc attribute does not exist.

When the framework passes non-zero selinux_flags to
selinux_android_setcontext2(), the setselinux_flags() call opens the
missing proc file and fails with ENOENT, which propagates as a fatal
error that aborts the Zygote child -- crashing every app at fork time
and leaving the device with a black screen.

Gracefully skip the selinux_flags write when the proc attribute is
absent (ENOENT) rather than treating it as a fatal error.  The
security hardening simply becomes a no-op on kernels without support,
which matches the intended behaviour documented in SELinuxFlags.java.
---
 libselinux/src/android/android_device.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libselinux/src/android/android_device.c b/libselinux/src/android/android_device.c
index e18d15a..b3c3769 100644
--- a/libselinux/src/android/android_device.c
+++ b/libselinux/src/android/android_device.c
@@ -134,8 +134,16 @@ int selinux_android_setcontext2(uid_t uid,
 	if (selinux_flags != 0) {
 		snprintf(buf_for_hex_uint64, sizeof buf_for_hex_uint64, "%" PRIx64 , selinux_flags);

-		 rc = setselinux_flags(buf_for_hex_uint64);
-		if (rc < 0)
+		rc = setselinux_flags(buf_for_hex_uint64);
+		if (rc < 0 && errno == ENOENT) {
+			/* Kernel does not support the selinux_flags proc
+			 * attribute (requires GrapheneOS kernel patches).
+			 * Silently skip -- the hardening features backed by
+			 * these flags simply won't be enforced. */
+			selinux_log(SELINUX_WARNING,
+				"%s: kernel lacks selinux_flags support, skipping\n",
+				__FUNCTION__);
+		} else if (rc < 0)
 			goto err;
 	}

